      "summary": "Mijbil the Otter is Gavin Maxwell's affectionate account of life with an otter. Lonely at Camusfearna in the Scottish Highlands after his pet dog died, Maxwell decided to keep an otter because the water around his house suited one. From Basra in Iraq, early in 1956, two Arabs brought him Mijbil, later identified as Maxwell's otter (Lutrogale perspicillata maxwelli), a race previously unknown to science and known only from Iraq. The chapter follows Mij's play with the bathroom tap, ping-pong balls and marbles, the nightmare journey to England in a nailed tin box, the chaos when he ran loose on the aircraft, the air hostess's kindness, the taxi and hotel stop in Paris, the amused customs officer in England, and the settlement at Camusfearna. Questions come from the tap scene, the tin box, the flight and Mijbil's character.",
