          "heading": "About the Author and Setting",
          "para": "Gavin Maxwell was a Scottish writer and naturalist, celebrated for Ring of Bright Water, and he lived at Camusfearna, a house in the Scottish Highlands that was ringed by water a few yards from its door. When his pet dog died, Maxwell found the loneliness of the house without a pet unbearable. Instead of getting another dog, he decided to keep an otter, an unusual choice made sensible by geography: the water all around Camusfearna would suit an otter perfectly, for otters are musteline mammals of the family Mustelidae, famous for their playful love of water. The chapter is the record of that experiment - part diary, part comedy, part love letter to an animal - and it opens with the author travelling south to find the creature who would share his life.",
