          "para": "When it was time to return to England, trouble began. The airline refused to carry the otter on the flight to London as he was; Mij could fly only if packed in a box not more than eighteen inches square, to be carried on the floor some distance from the author's seat. Maxwell therefore booked a passage to Paris on another airline, planning to complete the journey to England by train and bus. He got a tin box about eighteen inches square, made holes in it for air and nailed it shut with Mij inside shortly before the flight. When he opened the box, he found that the otter had clawed the lining to shreds in his frantic struggle to escape and had hurt himself, his paws bloody. The author, stricken with guilt, rushed to help the injured animal and opened the box - and on board, Mij suddenly darted out and disappeared down the aircraft, turning a careful plan into comedy.",
