          "para": "The question pattern for this chapter is stable and predictable. Extract-based questions draw on three set-pieces: the bathroom tap scene, the tin-box episode and the flight chaos. One and two-markers test names and places - Basra, Camusfearna, Paris - the year 1956, and the scientific name Lutrogale perspicillata maxwelli. Character questions demand Mijbil's traits, each proved by an incident; the examiner expects adjectives such as intelligent, playful, curious, mischievous and affectionate with evidence. Emotion questions probe the author's feelings - guilt over the injured otter, panic in the aircraft, delight in its games - and humour questions ask which episodes are funny and why. Theme questions may ask what the story says about keeping unusual pets or about the human-animal bond, and value questions highlight kindness to animals and responsible pet care. The winning method everywhere is to tie a quote or incident to a trait or theme in one tight sentence.",
