          "para": "The story's most celebrated moment arrives without warning. On the way to town, a young cow came galloping wildly in front of the bus, its tail held high; the driver sounded his horn again and again, but the more he honked the faster the frightened animal ran, so that it became a comic race. Valli laughed until there were tears in her eyes. On the return journey, at the same stretch of road, the bus slowed as it passed the same cow - now lying dead by the roadside, a motionless heap, evidently struck down by some fast-moving vehicle. The sight quenched Valli's joy in an instant; the animal whose antics had made her weep with laughter now lay lifeless, and she no longer wanted to look out of the window. In one afternoon, without a word of preaching, Valli meets the oldest truth of life: joy and sorrow travel the same road, and death can end laughter at any moment.",
