          "para": "The bus reached the town, and Valli took in the sights - the shops, the glittering wares, the crowds of strangers - all from her seat, for she had no intention of getting down and getting lost. When the conductor offered her a cold drink, she declined: she had no money to spare, her sixty paise having gone on the fares, and she would not spend a paisa beyond the plan. She stayed on board, drinking in the town through the window like a queen surveying her kingdom, and the bus began the journey back to her village. Then came the dead cow, and her gladness died with it. She reached home before anyone could mark her absence, slipped in quietly, and found her mother awake and chatting with one of her aunts, remarking that there were so many things in the world that no one could ever know about everything. Valli agreed knowingly, and her secret remained her own.",
