      "summary": "The Proposal by Anton Chekhov is a one-act farce set in the drawing-room of Chubukov's country house. Ivan Vassilevitch Lomov, a thirty-five-year-old neighbour and hypochondriac plagued by palpitations, comes to propose to twenty-five-year-old Natalya Stepanovna. Before he can state his purpose, the pair quarrel over Oxen Meadows, a small piece of land worth perhaps 300 roubles, and Lomov leaves. Recalled after Chubukov reveals the proposal, they instantly quarrel again over their dogs, Squeezer (85 roubles) and Guess (125 roubles), until Lomov collapses. In the confusion Chubukov joins their hands and declares them engaged, and the play ends with the wedding still pending and another dog-argument still running. Chekhov satirises marriage as economics and the pettiness of the landed gentry.",
