          "para": "This chapter is examined mainly through extracts and character questions. Extract-based items most often come from the Oxen Meadows quarrel or the dog quarrel, with occasional passages from the fainting scene and the ending; sub-questions ask for the speaker, the context, the cause of the quarrel and the irony. One-markers test prices, ages and names: 300 roubles for the Meadows, 85 roubles for Squeezer, 125 roubles for Guess, twenty-five and thirty-five for the couple. Character questions ask for sketches of Lomov, Natalya or Chubukov, each trait backed by an incident. Genre questions ask why the play is a farce and which devices create the comedy; theme questions probe marriage as a property arrangement and human pettiness; and value questions may ask what the play teaches about anger, communication and relationships. The reliable method: identify the quarrel, quote one short line, name the trait it exposes, and end by linking back to the proposal the quarrel delays.",
